From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: the programs that start at sign-in (Run keys and Startup folders)

Nothing started a person's startup programs in a Stained Glass session:
wineboot runs the Run keys and Startup folders only when it boots a
prefix, and the session's shared prefix is booted by the system. Tray
programs -- AmbirScan's, athenaNet Device Manager's, DYMO's, Greenshot --
never started at sign-in (David 2026-10-01, field report item 8: no
AmbirScan icon in the notification area, as on Windows).

The shell now does what Windows' does at sign-in, once: the person's
RunOnce (each value removed as it runs, "!name" after), the machine's Run
key in both registry views and the person's, then everyone's and the
person's Startup folder -- skipping what Task Manager's Startup tab turned
off (StartupApproved, first byte odd, as sg-shell's Task Manager writes).
Once per sign-in: XDG_SESSION_ID is kept in a volatile key, so an explorer
restarted in the same session starts nothing twice. Only the shell desktop
("shell"), not an elevated program's.

Gate: test/startup-gate.sh (mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_STARTUP,
SG_MUTANT_STARTUP_EVERY_TIME fail it).
---
--- a/programs/explorer/Makefile.in
+++ b/programs/explorer/Makefile.in
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 	fileexplorer.c \
 	fileprops.c \
 	startmenu.c \
+	startup.c \
 	shellkeys.c \
 	systray.c \
 	taskpins.c \
--- a/programs/explorer/desktop.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/desktop.c
@@ -3153,6 +3153,7 @@
 
         initialize_systray( using_root, enable_shell, show_systray, no_tray_items );
         if (enable_shell) initialize_autoplay();
+        if (enable_shell && !using_root) run_startup_programs();
         if (!using_root && enable_launchers) initialize_launchers( hwnd );
 
         if ((shell32 = LoadLibraryW( L"shell32.dll" )) &&
--- a/programs/explorer/explorer_private.h
+++ b/programs/explorer/explorer_private.h
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 extern void manage_desktop( WCHAR *arg );
 extern void initialize_systray( BOOL using_root, BOOL enable_shell, BOOL show_systray, BOOL no_tray_items );
 extern void initialize_appbar(void);
+extern void run_startup_programs(void);   /* Stained Glass OS: Run keys and Startup folders, once per sign-in */
 extern void handle_parent_notify( HWND hwnd, WPARAM wp );
 extern void shell_shutdown_dialog(void);   /* Stained Glass OS: Alt+F4 on the desktop or the taskbar */
 
--- /dev/null
+++ b/programs/explorer/startup.c
@@ -0,0 +1,218 @@
+/*
+ * Stained Glass OS: the programs that start when a person signs in
+ *
+ * As Windows' shell does at sign-in, once: the Run keys (the machine's, in
+ * both registry views, and the person's), the person's RunOnce (each value
+ * removed as it runs), and the Startup folders (everyone's and the
+ * person's) -- those the person has not turned off in Task Manager's Startup
+ * tab (StartupApproved: a value whose first byte is odd). Nothing ran them in
+ * a Stained Glass session -- wineboot does only when it boots a prefix, and
+ * the session's prefix is booted by the system: tray programs such as
+ * AmbirScan's, athenaNet Device Manager's or DYMO's never started at sign-in
+ * (David 2026-10-01).
+ *
+ * Once per sign-in: an explorer that starts again in the same session (it
+ * crashed, or was restarted) does not start them twice. The sign-in is told
+ * by XDG_SESSION_ID, kept in a volatile key (gone with the wineserver, at
+ * the latest when the machine restarts).
+ *
